    "page": 4,
    "bbox": {
      "l": 95.8,
      "t": 422.38,
      "r": 540.01,
      "b": 335.87
    },
    "text": "Recall that, if we consider n dimensional input, then g ( x ) = w T x ≥ w 0 . Therefore, in nth dimension, the decision boundary is a hyperplane with an intercept term w 0 . However, when we rewrite the equation in n +1 th dimension, then g ( x ) = w T x ≥ 0 is a hyperplane passing through the origin.",
    "artifact_path": null
  },
  {
    "index": 64,
    "type": "ListItem",
    "label": "list_item",
    "page": 4,
    "bbox": {
      "l": 79.02,
      "t": 320.64,
      "r": 540.0,
      "b": 254.3
    },
    "text": "(1 point) In the diagram shown below, the blue data points belong to positive class ( w T x ≥ 0) and red data points belong to negative class ( w T x < 0). The number of misclassified data points according to the decision line as shown in the figure is?",
    "artifact_path": null
  },
